{
  "_comment": [
    "The alignment pairs Scripture Pipelines supports, per R2 in",
    "project/plans/design-scripture-alignments.md (LLMFlow#238). This file is the declaration;",
    "Clear/Alignments/data/catalog.tsv is not read, because it describes a different tree",
    "(19 rows, one of which names a file that still exists) and arrives as a Git LFS pointer",
    "on a fresh clone.",
    "",
    "`dataset` names the registered dataset every path below is relative to. The declaration",
    "says which files serve a pair; the datasets store says where the corpus lives on this",
    "machine. Neither half carries a path that is wrong on someone else's machine.",
    "",
    "Each pair is validated at read time against the alignment file's declared `documents` and",
    "`roles`. That check is what catches a file whose name contradicts its contents, so a row",
    "here is a claim the engine verifies rather than trusts.",
    "",
    "Eighteen pairs. The corpus holds twenty-one alignment files, and the three that are not",
    "named here are omitted because their identifiers do not join, which a declaration cannot",
    "repair. Each was measured, not guessed:",
    "",
    "  hau WLCM-OHCB  declares the pair its SBLGNT sibling declares and is byte-identical to",
    "                 it, so there is no Hausa Old Testament alignment to name (Clear#12).",
    "  eng BGNT-BSB   target ids are 12 characters where nt_BSB.tsv has 11, so 0 of 172,736",
    "                 join. Dropping the trailing character reaches 99.86%, but 240 ids then",
    "                 name rows nt_BSB.tsv does not have. SBLGNT-BSB covers Greek to BSB.",
    "  fra WLCM-LSG   ot_LSG.tsv is 66 bytes, a header row and no data, so the French Old",
    "                 Testament target text is absent and 0 of 203,597 join.",
    "",
    "A pair named here is one whose identifiers were verified to join on both sides. Omitting",
    "the others means a request for one is refused by name rather than answered with silence.",
    "",
    "`process` records how the alignment was produced. Seventeen are hand aligned; por/JFA11 is",
    "machine-transferred, which is a difference a consumer weighing an alignment may want."
  ],
  "dataset": "clear-alignments",
